course: dictionary
lesson: 3526
title: Fe: a symbol, a Spanish word, and a fragment
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Fe is not an ordinary English word. In chemistry it is a symbol, a short code for a chemical element, and it always starts with a capital letter. «Each element has a short symbol: Na for sodium, Cl for chlorine, Fe for iron, Au for gold.» The other symbols in that sentence are clues, so Fe must be the code for iron.
explain: Fe comes from an old Latin name. «Fe» comes from «ferrum», the Latin word for iron. Some symbols match their English names, but others, like Fe and Au, come from older names, so you have to learn them.
explain: Look at the words around Fe. Next to a periodic table, a formula or a magnet, it means iron. In a Spanish sentence, it means faith. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence and seeing if it still makes sense.
explain: Fe is also a piece of longer words, such as «fee» and «female». Those are different words, so do not read them as the symbol for iron. Context tells you which meaning is right.
fact: Fe is the chemical symbol for iron, a metal element.
fact: Iron is element number 26 on the periodic table.
fact: Iron rusts in water and air, and rust contains Fe, as in Fe2O3.
fact: Fe comes from «ferrum», the Latin word for iron.
fact: In Spanish and Portuguese, «fe» means faith, but it is not an English word.
exercise: «Each element has a short symbol: Na for sodium, Cl for chlorine, Fe for iron, Au for gold.» Which element does Fe stand for? | Chlorine | Gold | Sodium | *Iron
exercise: Fe comes from «ferrum», the Latin word for iron. What language is ferrum from? | Greek | *Latin | English | Spanish
exercise: Maria says, «Ten fe en ti», which is Spanish. What does fe mean there? | Female | *Faith | A fee to pay | Iron
test: What is the chemical symbol for iron? | Ir | Ag | Ni | *Fe
test: In the word «fee», the letters fe are: | A symbol for iron, so fee means iron | *Just a fragment of a longer word, not the symbol | A Spanish word for faith | The Latin word for iron
exam: Which statement about «Fe» is true? | Fe can only ever mean faith | *Fe is the symbol for iron, and in Spanish it can mean faith | Fe is a girl's name in English | Fe is element number 2 on the periodic table
